# Derived by hand from Appendix B (`!Present` fires `unit` for a value that is present) and Type System ch. 4 (the call in the plain function is not lifted; `Seven` is lifted over its firing); R3: `$count` reads its value before the tick, so the first press gives `0 -? 1`, nothing, and the second `1 -? 1`, present. Never run.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="press")
    1: Ui.Label(text="0: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="1: 7")
